                        "sense_id": "d9e70784-3263-3ea7-a533-bae0be91ca86",
                        "entry_id": "bd363234-da20-3227-9ccc-17633ecd96fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A surname originating as an occupation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "45c1a350-9c50-335d-9c76-83e0704d2a41",
                        "entry_id": "bd363234-da20-3227-9ccc-17633ecd96fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A male given name transferred from the surname."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3006b756-8ff4-41c1-92c8-ea7d608b94c8",
                                "sense_id": "45c1a350-9c50-335d-9c76-83e0704d2a41",
                                "text": "\"My Dad wanted to name me Mats.\" \"But your Mom won,\" Carmen said, \"and named you after a movie star. Moms get away with murder. Mine, you probably think, named me after the girl in the opera.\" \"Tell you the truth,\" Wayne said, \"I never thought about it.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4367951c-dbc7-4dbb-adca-6561da8a9fb6",
                                "sense_id": "45c1a350-9c50-335d-9c76-83e0704d2a41",
                                "text": "Marcella and Nathaniel. Now I know their names. I haven't thought much about having children, but if I did, I wouldn't give them names like that. They're the sort of names you choose if you think you're someone to be reckoned with. I wonder if this is my Reverse L'Oréal Syndrome kicking in again; what would I call my kids, Wayne and Tracey? Because I'm not worth it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93fb5ff8-601c-4755-a327-e7168230a314",
                                "sense_id": "45c1a350-9c50-335d-9c76-83e0704d2a41",
                                "text": "The testimony of Wayne LaPierre, in the waning days of his long tenure as head of one of the nation’s most powerful lobbying groups, could highlight a New York civil trial alleging top officials used the National Rifle Association as a “personal piggy bank.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
